
ABORT(3F)           UNIX Programmer's Manual            ABORT(3F)

NAME
     abort - terminate abruptly with memory image

SYNOPSIS
     subroutine abort (string)
     character*(*) string

DESCRIPTION
     _A_b_o_r_t cleans up the I/O buffers and then aborts producing a
     _c_o_r_e file in the current directory.  If _s_t_r_i_n_g is given, it
     is written to logical unit 0 preceeded by ``abort:''.

FILES
     /usr/lib/libF77.a

SEE ALSO
     abort(3)

BUGS
     _S_t_r_i_n_g is ignored on the PDP11.

